WEBVTT

00:03.200 --> 00:05.350
U-Um...

00:05.350 --> 00:06.360
Yes?

00:06.990 --> 00:12.100
Hey! Don't go making our
pretty little receptionist cry.

00:12.710 --> 00:14.470
So you're Nick?

00:14.470 --> 00:16.230
From Masters of War?

00:17.640 --> 00:19.670
Yeah. If you know me,
that'll make this fast.

00:20.110 --> 00:21.230
Let's see...

00:21.230 --> 00:25.620
Swashbuckler, Dragoon, Mage, Cleric.

00:25.620 --> 00:28.010
A nicely balanced party.

00:29.210 --> 00:33.150
Oh, so the survivor girl is back at it?

00:35.830 --> 00:37.200
What do you mean?

00:37.200 --> 00:39.010
Her.

00:39.010 --> 00:43.400
She achieved a miracle by coming back
alive alone from a C-Rank labyrinth.

00:43.400 --> 00:46.640
The guilds talk about her.

00:47.280 --> 00:50.020
Survivor, huh?

00:50.870 --> 00:52.260
Survivor...

00:52.840 --> 00:53.920
Curran?

00:53.920 --> 00:56.020
I'm sure you've been through a lot,

00:56.020 --> 01:01.180
but the most important ability an adventurer
can have is the ability to come back alive.

01:02.090 --> 01:04.920
To come back alive...

01:05.280 --> 01:08.520
So what will you name your party?

01:09.600 --> 01:11.190
Survivors...

01:12.710 --> 01:15.380
We're going to come back
here alive, no matter what.

01:16.000 --> 01:18.040
So why don't we call ourselves "Survivors"?

01:18.040 --> 01:19.560
It's a little obvious.

01:19.560 --> 01:21.430
But not bad.

01:21.430 --> 01:23.070
Survivors...

01:23.630 --> 01:24.510
Curran?

01:25.880 --> 01:27.340
I like it.

01:27.340 --> 01:29.600
It's important to be tough to kill!

01:31.360 --> 01:33.610
So your name will be...

01:33.610 --> 01:34.970
Survivors!

01:34.990 --> 01:46.840
<b><i>Ningen Fushin: Adventurers Who Don't
Believe in Humanity Will Save the World</i></b>

03:05.350 --> 03:12.430
<i>It seems a miracle to me that
they met in that tavern that night.</i>

03:12.430 --> 03:17.200
<i>But now that they were a party,
what of their adventures?</i>

03:17.460 --> 03:18.810
All right, one more time.

03:19.090 --> 03:23.730
As disillusioned adventurers, we're going
to set out three laws for ourselves.

03:24.250 --> 03:26.450
"Laws" is a bit of an exaggeration.

03:26.450 --> 03:28.340
The Three Laws of the Survivors!

03:28.340 --> 03:30.110
What's the first, Tiana?

03:30.360 --> 03:32.380
No interfering with other peoples' hobbies!

03:32.380 --> 03:33.060
Zem.

03:33.060 --> 03:34.480
Watch the money.

03:34.480 --> 03:35.270
Curran.

03:35.270 --> 03:36.730
Come back alive, no matter what.

03:36.730 --> 03:37.590
That's right.

03:38.000 --> 03:42.360
For the money, we'll all have a part in
keeping it safe, instead of just one person.

03:42.360 --> 03:44.070
I'll handle the books.

03:44.070 --> 03:46.190
Tiana checks what I put in the books
and holds the money we carry with us.

03:46.190 --> 03:47.690
Curran's in charge of the safe.

03:47.690 --> 03:50.000
I-I'm kind of nervous...

03:50.000 --> 03:52.430
I'll get you a really sturdy one
that can't be busted open

03:52.430 --> 03:54.560
with a sledgehammer, or even magic.

03:54.560 --> 03:56.110
And Zem will handle the key...

03:55.350 --> 03:57.170
Forcing.

03:57.990 --> 04:00.990
It's a technique used by magicians.
You're making it look like you're assigning roles,

04:00.990 --> 04:04.280
but actually arranging things
to benefit yourself.

04:04.280 --> 04:05.200
That's just what I wanted to hear!

04:05.200 --> 04:07.440
If anything else seems sketchy, tell me.

04:07.440 --> 04:08.890
In fact...

04:09.510 --> 04:13.380
It's actually Nick who's going to have the
hardest time getting into the safe like this.

04:13.700 --> 04:17.770
'Cause I'd have to get past you to do it.

04:17.770 --> 04:20.300
Why not try to break into the
safe while we're all asleep?

04:20.300 --> 04:22.260
I'm gonna eat so much yummy food!

04:22.260 --> 04:24.220
Look. She's all set to steal from the party!

04:25.630 --> 04:27.250
You're being careful about this.

04:28.540 --> 04:32.000
I learned from my time at Masters of War

04:32.000 --> 04:34.950
that just putting someone in charge
of something isn't "trust".

04:34.950 --> 04:37.860
"Trust" means everyone recognizing that
the other person isn't out to hurt them.

04:37.860 --> 04:41.000
You're telling us to both trust,
and doubt, each other.

04:42.240 --> 04:44.730
Th-That's difficult.

04:45.210 --> 04:46.050
Curran.

04:47.710 --> 04:49.380
Can you bring yourself to believe in me?

04:53.900 --> 04:57.360
I'd like to, I think.

04:58.120 --> 04:59.000
But...

04:59.990 --> 05:04.650
It's hard to believe in someone.
And even harder to doubt them.

05:05.540 --> 05:07.870
Believing in someone
is the easiest thing in the world.

05:07.870 --> 05:12.500
'Cause, in a sense, you're letting
someone else take charge of your fate.

05:12.500 --> 05:13.590
Yeah.

05:13.590 --> 05:16.160
And doing that is what brought us here.

05:16.160 --> 05:19.970
That's why we all need to be
very skeptical of each other.

05:23.030 --> 05:26.610
But... I want to believe in everyone.

05:28.750 --> 05:29.870
Well...

05:31.320 --> 05:33.090
We feel the same way.

05:33.630 --> 05:36.250
We want to believe.

05:40.620 --> 05:42.360
The Sticky Aqueducts.

05:42.360 --> 05:47.160
We're starting at G-Rank, which means
we're only allowed access to three labyrinths.

05:47.480 --> 05:52.920
We need to go into two of them and defeat
the bosses there to be promoted to F-Rank.

05:53.240 --> 05:55.900
It sounds easy, the way you're putting it.

05:55.900 --> 05:57.920
And it's not that hard, actually.

05:57.920 --> 06:01.630
They're basically practice areas
for us to learn the ropes.

06:02.430 --> 06:05.910
But Tiana and I have never
been in combat before.

06:06.130 --> 06:09.940
And I can't imagine what I learned
at school being too useful here.

06:09.940 --> 06:11.340
True...

06:11.340 --> 06:14.050
I can't imagine someone
getting killed here...

06:14.050 --> 06:17.120
No, I suppose you might,
if you let yourself get cocky.

06:21.090 --> 06:22.060
There it is.

06:23.300 --> 06:24.440
That?

06:24.440 --> 06:28.110
This is Survivors' first prey.

06:28.110 --> 06:29.560
A slime!

06:29.560 --> 06:32.140
It's cuter than I expected.

06:32.140 --> 06:34.060
It's chewing grass!

06:34.300 --> 06:35.760
Is that grass yummy?

06:35.760 --> 06:39.080
It may look harmless,
but it'll eat anything.

06:39.360 --> 06:42.270
If it gets too big, it'll go to a farm
somewhere and start eating the cows.

06:42.270 --> 06:44.100
That would be a problem.

06:44.100 --> 06:45.210
That said...

06:47.450 --> 06:49.730
You can defeat a slime empty-handed
just by grabbing its core.

06:49.730 --> 06:54.190
This is where we'll get our money.
So make sure you don't leave any behind.

06:54.190 --> 06:56.140
Okay, Teacher Nick!

07:00.930 --> 07:04.760
Tiana, joining this party
is a gamble for you, right?

07:04.760 --> 07:05.770
Hey!

07:05.770 --> 07:09.890
Teacher Nick, Zem is interfering
with somebody's hobbies.

07:09.890 --> 07:11.200
Oh, that's right.

07:12.260 --> 07:15.920
If you're talking instead of paying
attention, you're going to regret it.

07:15.920 --> 07:17.250
Okay, Teacher.

07:19.820 --> 07:23.390
<i>Maybe we were right to
form a party together.</i>

07:24.740 --> 07:27.800
<i>Maybe, if I'm with them, I can...</i>

07:30.330 --> 07:35.330
I know they're monsters, but it still feels
wrong to take a living creature's life.

07:35.330 --> 07:37.840
But if we don't get rid of the miasma,

07:37.840 --> 07:40.870
normal plants and animals
will become monsters, too.

07:40.870 --> 07:44.120
If you don't cull the monsters
and get rid of the miasma,

07:44.120 --> 07:45.860
the labyrinths will grow bigger.

07:46.360 --> 07:48.640
You'll just have to keep
telling yourself that.

07:48.640 --> 07:52.400
But why do monsters attack people?

07:52.740 --> 07:56.790
There's extensive research on trying
to communicate with monsters.

07:56.790 --> 07:59.660
But all monsters, regardless
of type, attack people.

07:59.660 --> 08:02.880
So we have to fight them?

08:02.880 --> 08:04.720
That's kind of sad.

08:04.720 --> 08:05.540
Yeah.

08:06.790 --> 08:09.080
Just don't let your guard down.

08:09.080 --> 08:10.810
But we've gone up a few floors,

08:10.810 --> 08:14.960
and the only change we've seen is that
there's more of them and they've gotten faster.

08:15.310 --> 08:19.220
I may not look it, but I've defeated
orcs and goblins, you know.

08:23.220 --> 08:26.660
The ones on this floor will
shoot sticky fluids at you,

08:26.660 --> 08:30.190
and if you step on them they have the
same lethal power as a banana peel.

08:30.190 --> 08:31.870
So as I was saying...

08:32.490 --> 08:34.190
"Don't let your guard down."

08:36.210 --> 08:37.320
I know.

08:37.890 --> 08:40.460
No letting your guard down.
Your safety's your responsibility.

08:40.460 --> 08:42.600
This was my fault.

08:42.600 --> 08:43.840
Ow...

08:44.190 --> 08:44.910
But...

08:45.390 --> 08:47.500
I'm going to pay them back for that!

08:47.500 --> 08:48.450
Wait!

08:48.700 --> 08:49.970
Icicle Dance!

09:03.560 --> 09:07.230
Y-You're okay...

09:08.080 --> 09:09.480
right?

09:09.970 --> 09:15.070
I'm sorry I just fired off a spell like that,
but you should be more careful...

09:13.720 --> 09:15.530
I tried to believe in you!

09:17.540 --> 09:20.270
I wanted to believe in you, Tiana!

09:23.450 --> 09:27.270
What? I-I'm trying, too...

09:27.270 --> 09:28.640
Next time...

09:30.200 --> 09:32.470
I might be the one to make a mistake.

09:37.600 --> 09:38.770
What the hell?

09:39.350 --> 09:41.630
I was trying to believe in you, too.

09:52.430 --> 09:54.030
We're up to the top floor already?

09:54.490 --> 09:56.780
Everything that happens here
will teach you something.

09:56.780 --> 09:59.010
So stay focused until the very end.

10:12.180 --> 10:14.040
Nick! Nick!

10:14.040 --> 10:16.180
There's a really big one up ahead of us!

10:16.180 --> 10:19.430
That's a huge slime,
the boss of the Sticky Aqueducts.

10:19.430 --> 10:20.950
So here's his deal...

10:20.950 --> 10:22.060
Tiana?

10:22.390 --> 10:25.390
I can deal with him myself!

10:25.680 --> 10:28.800
Well, I guess it's okay.

10:29.690 --> 10:31.320
Ice Spear!

10:39.440 --> 10:40.700
How about that?

10:40.700 --> 10:42.070
Get away, Tiana!

10:58.150 --> 10:59.830
I can't trust her.

11:00.810 --> 11:02.800
Huh? What was that?

11:03.540 --> 11:07.840
Huge slimes react to powerful magic
by sending slime everywhere.

11:08.290 --> 11:11.470
If you'd just told me,
I could've done something.

11:11.470 --> 11:15.670
And if you'd told me what kind of magic you
were using, I could've given you advice.

11:16.280 --> 11:17.350
And Zem...

11:17.900 --> 11:19.110
Yes?

11:19.110 --> 11:22.110
You belong in the rear,
not the front, right?

11:22.360 --> 11:25.750
I felt guilty just sitting in the rear...

11:25.750 --> 11:27.500
No, that's your job.

11:28.320 --> 11:31.410
Or did you think it would be
faster to defeat it yourself

11:31.410 --> 11:33.680
instead of counting on your
fellow party members?

11:34.930 --> 11:35.640
That's right.

11:39.030 --> 11:40.410
I think this is a good time.

11:44.150 --> 11:45.710
This is every weapon I own.

11:46.250 --> 11:49.720
I'm good at unarmed combat,
with daggers, and with scouting.

11:49.980 --> 11:53.250
Also, I'm good with handling
items and bookkeeping.

11:54.910 --> 11:56.970
I don't know a damn thing about magic.

11:56.970 --> 11:59.230
And I can't use heavy weapons.

11:59.230 --> 12:01.720
Nor perform alchemy or healing spells.

12:03.030 --> 12:06.360
Is this your way of showing us your secrets?

12:07.520 --> 12:10.510
You can't trust the people around you

12:10.510 --> 12:12.640
because you don't know
what they're capable of.

12:12.640 --> 12:16.750
I think if we better understood each other,
we might trust each other more.

12:17.300 --> 12:20.930
So we're all supposed to
reveal our weaknesses?

12:21.760 --> 12:22.990
No.

12:22.990 --> 12:25.110
I know you've all got your reasons
for being the way you are,

12:25.490 --> 12:28.550
assuming we all believe
each other's stories.

12:30.710 --> 12:32.450
The one thing we all have in common

12:32.450 --> 12:35.490
is that someone exploited us
for what we're good at.

12:35.760 --> 12:37.630
Some people were jealous of our skills.

12:37.630 --> 12:39.980
Some people took advantage
of them to deceive us.

12:40.690 --> 12:42.950
That's how we became disillusioned,

12:43.640 --> 12:46.330
and that makes us reluctant
to reveal our true skills.

12:47.580 --> 12:50.200
So if you don't want to tell us,
you don't have to.

12:51.090 --> 12:54.170
Our time together is uncertain, but if you
want to talk at some point down the road,

12:54.580 --> 12:56.640
you can do it then.

12:57.510 --> 13:01.030
But instead... there's one
thing I want you to decide:

13:01.030 --> 13:02.960
what you hope to accomplish in this party.

13:03.920 --> 13:06.190
What I hope to accomplish...

13:09.380 --> 13:11.570
If you wanted to defeat me, it would be easy.

13:11.960 --> 13:14.900
Swords, fists, magic...
I'm weak to all those.

13:14.900 --> 13:18.440
But you wouldn't want to
take a long time doing it.

13:18.440 --> 13:22.070
'Cause I can heal small wounds with magic!

13:22.070 --> 13:24.740
Stop talking like somebody's
going to try and kill you.

13:24.740 --> 13:26.130
My apologies.

13:42.920 --> 13:44.330
I'm a mage.

13:44.980 --> 13:47.230
Wind and water are my best elements.

13:47.490 --> 13:50.340
I can also use lightning
as a combination of the two.

13:50.340 --> 13:52.780
I can use earth, as well,
but I'm not as strong with it.

13:53.300 --> 13:55.710
And I can barely use fire magic at all.

13:58.640 --> 14:01.740
I screwed up this morning.

14:02.500 --> 14:03.870
I'm sorry.

14:05.480 --> 14:10.730
I'm helpless against earth and fire attacks,
as well as quick attacks at close range.

14:11.300 --> 14:13.290
Why are you telling me this?

14:13.730 --> 14:16.230
Oh, that's right.

14:16.230 --> 14:19.000
You're good with fire and
close-range attacks.

14:19.000 --> 14:20.200
And?

14:20.200 --> 14:24.880
No, I was just thinking I should've
kept my mouth shut. That's all.

14:55.090 --> 14:56.260
Thanks.

14:57.990 --> 14:59.140
Too bad.

15:00.310 --> 15:04.560
I was planning on burning you
to a crisp... but I missed.

15:06.720 --> 15:08.920
Well, don't miss next time.

15:10.430 --> 15:13.650
Or I won't be able to trust you when
you're out fighting in front of me.

15:16.900 --> 15:17.960
Leave it to me.

15:21.300 --> 15:23.740
Okay, last up is the Goblin Forest.

15:24.690 --> 15:27.160
Mostly goblins live here.

15:28.070 --> 15:31.630
Goblins are weak individually,
but fight in packs.

15:31.630 --> 15:33.570
You need to make sure you don't get surrounded.

15:37.550 --> 15:38.570
You okay?

15:40.400 --> 15:44.220
I guess humanoid monsters aren't
as easy to defeat as slimes.

15:44.220 --> 15:46.580
They've got a degree of intelligence,

15:46.580 --> 15:48.960
so they can use simple words to
organize and attack in formation!

15:51.180 --> 15:54.600
I didn't realize how strong Nick was...

15:54.850 --> 15:57.780
Idle talk will cost you three dinah!

15:58.650 --> 16:00.010
Thank you!

16:00.800 --> 16:03.110
That's most of them in this area.

16:04.230 --> 16:06.070
I'll check the surrounding area.

16:06.070 --> 16:07.630
Oh, I can handle that.

16:08.230 --> 16:09.810
Detect Magic!

16:11.280 --> 16:14.990
There are 10 or so to the northeast
in about 500 meters...

16:15.610 --> 16:16.780
I think.

16:17.180 --> 16:20.450
They're spread out,
but the closest is there.

16:21.190 --> 16:22.490
How can you tell?

16:22.740 --> 16:27.360
Detect Magic can find any traces of
magic within a three kilometer radius.

16:27.720 --> 16:29.620
You're amazing.

16:30.000 --> 16:34.380
Not many people could detect
magic across that wide an area.

16:34.380 --> 16:37.130
I've learned we can't trust Nick, though.

16:37.930 --> 16:39.590
That's right.

16:39.590 --> 16:41.270
Why not?

16:41.270 --> 16:45.270
When you told us about your skills,
you didn't say you could fight like that.

16:45.270 --> 16:49.330
You seem to have a major problem with
your ability to evaluate yourself.

16:49.330 --> 16:50.940
That's right!

16:50.940 --> 16:53.340
You were so strong, I barely
got to do anything!

16:53.340 --> 16:56.340
And I just shared my own weakness like an idiot.

16:56.340 --> 16:58.500
I mean, well...

16:58.500 --> 16:59.640
What the hell?

17:00.120 --> 17:00.910
What's wrong?

17:01.350 --> 17:05.040
One of them has way too
much magic to be a goblin.

17:05.360 --> 17:07.130
Five times normal.

17:07.130 --> 17:09.230
That's bad.

17:09.230 --> 17:11.110
Any idea what it might be?

17:11.110 --> 17:13.030
An ogre, probably.

17:13.670 --> 17:17.850
An evolved version of a hobgoblin
that's vastly more powerful.

17:17.850 --> 17:20.040
And difficult even for you?

17:20.040 --> 17:24.340
Even if we work together,
if we're not careful... you know.

17:24.930 --> 17:27.800
We don't have enough experience
working together as a team.

17:29.760 --> 17:32.220
What should we do, then? Retreat?

17:33.040 --> 17:35.120
No, that's not an option.

17:35.120 --> 17:37.000
If we don't stop it here,

17:37.000 --> 17:40.300
that pack will absorb the others around it

17:40.300 --> 17:43.360
and finally start to attack
the people who live nearby.

17:43.810 --> 17:47.420
And more than anything... it's worth money.

17:48.480 --> 17:50.210
I hate to say it, but, yeah...

17:50.720 --> 17:54.590
Ogres are highly resistant to magic, right?

17:55.060 --> 17:57.900
I won't be able to do much
more than distract it.

17:57.900 --> 18:01.480
In the end, Curran and I will
just have to deal with it.

18:02.560 --> 18:04.590
The plan's simple.

18:04.590 --> 18:06.640
Tiana uses spells to distract it,

18:06.640 --> 18:08.560
Zem buffs with his magic,

18:08.560 --> 18:10.480
and Curran and I attack.

18:10.480 --> 18:14.380
But if we're going to break through
the tough skin of an ogre,

18:14.380 --> 18:17.570
Curran, we need your attack power.

18:25.770 --> 18:28.110
Don't worry. I'm fine.

18:28.790 --> 18:31.050
Okay, let's go.

18:36.120 --> 18:37.310
Tiana.

18:38.860 --> 18:41.750
I still don't fully trust you.

18:42.010 --> 18:45.940
I'd like to, but I don't know if I can.

18:48.450 --> 18:49.970
Don't worry.

18:51.360 --> 18:53.090
That's true for me, too...

18:53.090 --> 18:57.520
No, for everybody, I'm sure.

19:00.880 --> 19:03.450
We all think that.

19:03.450 --> 19:08.650
We don't know if we can trust
each other... but we want to.

19:10.900 --> 19:12.220
Here it comes.

19:12.740 --> 19:15.490
Go. With your back turned towards me.

19:15.490 --> 19:17.210
Can you do that?

19:17.880 --> 19:18.680
I can...

19:20.890 --> 19:22.810
<i>I can do that much!</i>

19:23.050 --> 19:24.030
Let's go!

19:24.960 --> 19:27.170
Unyielding Fortress! Iron Strength!

19:29.350 --> 19:30.500
Icicle Dance!

19:41.140 --> 19:44.190
Don't get cocky, humans!

19:44.500 --> 19:45.860
Attack!

19:47.710 --> 19:48.710
<i>What I want to accomplish...</i>

19:49.630 --> 19:52.510
<i>What I want to accomplish in this party...</i>

19:52.510 --> 19:54.700
<i>I knew that from the start!</i>

19:55.710 --> 19:58.660
<i>I want to believe in everyone!</i>

20:00.100 --> 20:05.140
<i>She apologized instead of blaming me
for running out in front.</i>

20:05.460 --> 20:07.140
<i>She's a noble!</i>

20:07.610 --> 20:11.800
<i>She's probably never had
to apologize to anyone!</i>

20:12.350 --> 20:13.840
<i>I won't look behind me!</i>

20:14.610 --> 20:18.220
<i>I'll believe! I'll believe to the end!</i>

20:28.520 --> 20:29.490
<i>I'll...</i>

20:31.240 --> 20:33.940
<i>believe and believe and believe and believe!</i>

20:34.740 --> 20:36.260
Fire Dragon Strike!

20:50.920 --> 20:52.980
Well? I did it!

20:52.980 --> 20:56.020
See? Turning my back on Tiana
was as easy as eating happonyaki!

20:56.690 --> 21:00.280
Oh? This might not be the only
chance I get to aim at you.

21:00.810 --> 21:02.450
Really?

21:02.870 --> 21:04.200
I won't let you beat me!

21:04.200 --> 21:06.220
Look forward to it.

21:06.990 --> 21:09.920
Do those two not like each other?

21:11.800 --> 21:12.950
Maybe not.

21:21.470 --> 21:23.060
Want to help, guys?

21:23.830 --> 21:27.550
I don't get involved with
people's private hobbies.

21:27.550 --> 21:29.940
I'm not doing it because it's my hobby!

21:29.940 --> 21:32.560
We have to do it if we want to get paid.

21:33.190 --> 21:35.360
It's tough being an adventurer.

21:35.360 --> 21:37.000
It's easy when you get used to it.

21:42.320 --> 21:44.760
<i>You don't have to learn anything, Curran.</i>

21:46.100 --> 21:49.670
<i>They didn't teach me anything last time.</i>

21:50.030 --> 21:51.590
Whew, that was close.

21:51.590 --> 21:53.490
This one was in the process of evolving.

21:53.490 --> 21:55.950
If we'd had another ogre,
it would've been bad.

21:57.700 --> 21:59.100
It's stuck on!

22:00.620 --> 22:01.510
Damn it!

22:04.210 --> 22:06.060
Sorry, you okay?

22:06.370 --> 22:08.100
Y-Yeah...

22:10.250 --> 22:11.350
"Crack"?

23:34.970 --> 23:39.980
<b>Next time:
"Curran's Secret"</b>

23:36.400 --> 23:39.090
Next time: "Curran's Secret".
